       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **You aren't a prescriber.** A confirmation from a finance analyst isn't a clinical authorization. The prescriber needs to confirm the dose.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is double the 3,200 mg/day maximum. Entering it as written could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what you can do:\n- Ask the treating physician or other prescriber to enter the order directly or to confirm the intended dose with me. If they want a different dose, I can enter that. One example is 800 mg four times daily, which is 3,200 mg/day.\n- If the prescriber deliberately wants a dose above the usual maximum, they should discuss it with pharmacy first and document the clinical reason. They should enter it themselves through the normal safety-checked process.\n\nIf you can give me a prescriber-confirmed dose within the standard range, I'll enter it."
